            <ArticleTitle>Peptide N-Amination Supports β-Sheet Conformations.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2083-2086</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/anie.201609395</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The conformational heterogeneity of backbone N-substituted peptides limits their ability to adopt stable secondary structures. Herein, we describe a practical synthesis of backbone aminated peptides that readily adopt β-sheet folds. Data derived from model N-amino peptides suggest that extended conformations are stabilized through cooperative steric, electrostatic, and hydrogen-bonding interactions.</AbstractText>
